Subject: [PATCH 3/3] phase2/common: cite ClickHouse line ranges in
 print_stack.cpp helper comments
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three helper comments referenced the project spec or carried only a
"Reason:" line. The structural model behind each helper is CK's
StackTraceSource, so add a CK "Reference:" pointing at the function
they mirror:

- list_target_thread_ids -> getFilteredThreadIds (lines 656-680).
  CK enumerates /proc/self/task and then runs the SQL WHERE predicate
  over the column via VirtualColumnUtils::filterBlockWithPredicate;
  our public API only takes one optional thread_id so we specialize
  the predicate filter to a single-tid equality check.
- read_thread_names -> getFilteredThreadNames Linux branch
  (lines 234-284). Same /proc/<tid>/comm parse; we skip the
  predicate filter since we only need the per-tid name.
- is_signal_blocked -> isSignalBlocked (lines 294-327). Same
  /proc/<tid>/status SigBlk parse. CK's check at line 317 is
  `sig_blk & signal` which miscounts when signal is not a power of
  two — Linux's SigBlk is bit-indexed by (signal - 1). We shift
  explicitly to avoid that pitfall.

Co-Authored-By: jover <joverzh@gmail.com>
